              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Susan Weil"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I think the portions of grape juice and Cinnamon are totally off. There's no way it needs THAT much grape juice or cinnamon. And that little honey for that much apple. But once I poured off most of the grape juice and added much more honey, it's not bad.",
            "datePublished": "2021-03-29T03:38:59.280Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Debbie Clements Becker"
            },
            "reviewBody": "It is so good. I love that it doesn't use wine, I don't like my sister in laws (she uses the wine and I find it too sweet and syrupy) this has a light crisp flavor, I will be making it again...thinking nice sode dish on a hot summer day.",
            "datePublished": "2021-03-27T21:52:54.157Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "TXGaeilgesinger"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I had to make substitutions and estimate quantity for one person, but it came out so well that I ate the whole bit even though I had enough for 2. I used a Granny Smith apple, slivered almonds, a shot of Martinelli's apple juice, and a dash of Grade B Maple Syrup all mixed up together. Didn't take but about 10 minutes and most of that was hunting ingredients and cutting up the apple..DELICIOUS!!!!! I thought I'd use pistachios or pecans but couldn't find either successfully at the time and I had no walnuts, so I went with the almonds I had in the fridge. I will definitely make this again and hopefully by the given recipe just to do it.",
            "datePublished": "2020-04-15T18:02:21.527Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Cookie734"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Simple, easy Charoset. Kosher wine can be exchanged for grape juice, and pecans can be substituted for walnuts (either way, this recipe is easy and delicious). My apples and nuts were chunkier, rather than finely chopped.",
            "datePublished": "2013-02-27T14:36:33.547Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
